{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779301040,"nonce":"IHW5BQ9AxxmIn+nECWcBnwKwtDg=","title":"Umbrella: Studio/provider schema contract, task data, and selector validation","message":"## Problem\n\nFeedbax Studio now has enough scenario, task-boundary, objective, selector, metric, provider, and execution-preparation surface area that more UI polish will harden ad hoc assumptions unless the shared schema contract is made explicit.\n\nThe current state is split across several partial substrates:\n\n- Feedbax exposes provider manifests, registries, schemas, validation, execution preparation, and manifests through `c6c6da0` / `f68cf66` work.\n- Studio owns scenario projections, selectors, objectives, task bindings, metrics, and task timelines through `93f79f2`, `bd5aefb`, and related child issues.\n- Task-as-scenario-boundary work established that tasks are not ordinary graph components, but current type names and payload fields still say \"Task Output\".\n- Selector and metric slices improved the UI, but the remaining depth depends on provider-owned schema data rather than curated frontend hints.\n- Future Mandible integration under `fa3978f` needs Feedbax to expose coherent provider contracts rather than Studio-local or Mandible-specific assumptions.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Treat this as a Feedbax provider/schema overhaul with Studio as the first consumer.\n- Keep Mandible out of the implementation path for now; Mandible coherence comes from provider manifest/capability/schema discoverability and cross-links.\n- Rename Task Output terminology to Task Data everywhere in new Studio/provider contracts.\n- Keep `task_binding_spec` as the scenario field, but bump its schema version to `feedbax.studio.task_bindings.v2` because the payload field names intentionally break.\n- Define shared schema records before deep UI work: `ValueSchema`, `PortSchema`, `TaskDataSchema`, `SelectorTargetSchema`, `SchemaValidationIssue`, and `StudioSchemaRegistry`.\n- Add a provider-owned scenario schema enumeration service and HTTP endpoint.\n- Stage runtime PyTree/sample introspection after the static provider contract is stable.\n- Use child issues and feature worktrees, then merge upward into one integration branch and submit one final auth request to `develop`.\n\n## Child Issue Order\n\n1. Provider schema contract and Task Data rename.\n2. Static provider-owned schema enumeration.\n3. Graph and task-data validation integration.\n4. Schema-backed selector browser.\n5. Objective, probe, metric, and ValueSpec alignment.\n6. Optional runtime PyTree/sample introspection.\n7. Flexible intervention targeting over typed selector targets.\n\n## Related Issues\n\n- `fa3978f` — Feedbax/Mandible MVP integration roadmap.\n- `c6c6da0` — Feedbax manifests and provider contract.\n- `f68cf66` — Feedbax as Mandible provider/plugin.\n- `93f79f2` — Feedbax Studio design coordination.\n- `bd5aefb` — ValueSpec/task timeline umbrella.\n- `0258fac` — port constraints/type checking.\n- `0e1cd8c` — probe/metric nodes as loss targets.\n- `b3ad156` — flexible UI-driven state targeting.\n- `e57ae1f` — real Studio JAX training backend.\n- `d64a9aa` — environment/task protocol unification.\n- `c540499` — compact task params/lazy task generation.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Provider manifest exposes the new schema capability and schema models.\n- Studio task-binding payloads use Task Data terminology and reject old Task Output payload names clearly.\n- Static provider enumeration returns graph ports, task data, selector targets, and validation issues for active scenarios.\n- Graph connection and task-data binding validation consume provider schema data.\n- Selector/objective/metric surfaces consume `SelectorTargetSchema`/`ValueSchema` rather than curated-only hints.\n- Runtime introspection remains optional enrichment and does not block basic provider/Studio validation.\n- Final integration is submitted through one Mandible auth request to `develop`.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}